# A `fn` line carrying parameters and nothing under it. The parser holds a
# name and a parameter list with no statements to attach them to, so it
# refuses here rather than building a function that answers nothing.
#
# No golden pinned this message until now, and the gate built to catch that
# could not see it. The scan keeps a diagnostic's leading literal run — the
# text before the first interpolation — and required twelve characters of it.
# `function ` plus the backtick is ten, so the site was walked past and the
# corpus was reported complete.
fn nobody x

pub play = print "x"
